haracteristic of certain cell walls of some bacteria. DAP is often found in the peptide linkages of NAM-NAG chains that make up the cell wall of gram-negative bacteria. When provided, they exhibit normal growth. When in deficiency, they still grow but with the inability to make new cell wall peptidoglycan.\nThis is also the attachment point for Braun's lipoprotein.", "titolo": "Diaminopimelic acid", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diaminopimelic_acid"}}